Separately from that included source, the following parts of WikiLM were
written independently against obsidian-llm-wiki's published design, and this
NOTICE credits that design for each of them. The files marked * also credit it
in a comment at the point of use.

  - src/retrieval.ts*, src/askCheck.ts* — the seed-selection cascade
    (lexical, keyword, graph expansion), the title-over-body scoring weight,
    and answering from general knowledge with a label rather than refusing.

  - src/vaultLint.ts* — the vault scanners: orphans, dead links, empty pages,
    missing aliases.

  - src/vaultFix.ts*, src/modals.ts* — dead-link repair by tiered name
    resolution, and a lint report whose fix buttons are gated on counts.

  - src/topicNote.ts, src/suggestPlan.ts — filing new material into a section
    of an existing page, and creating that section when it is absent.

WikiLM's own commands follow WikiLM's policies where the two conflict:
notably, WikiLM's highlight digest and its AI highlight command append new
material into an existing page whenever one is related, rather than giving it
a page of its own unless an existing page denotes the same thing. WikiLM's two
ingest commands are the exception. They run the included obsidian-llm-wiki
engine and follow its policy, with a guard of WikiLM's between the engine and
the vault (src/upstream/guardedVault.ts): each existing page is saved before
it is overwritten, and a rewrite that would drop a page's headings, quotes,
PDF links, embeds or frontmatter keys is refused.
